WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.367
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:05.067
We are here with the one
and only Michelle Obama.

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:06.667
Now...

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:09.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.234
We're always so happy
you come on the show.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:14.701
Thank you very much.
I noticed that you went back --

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:17.801
you went back
to the White House recently.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:20.734
You haven't been back.
-No. Wasn't invited.

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:22.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.534
Ooh, shade.

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:29.567
-Wow. Wow.

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:33.300
I'm adding a chapter right here.
Hold on.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.434
-Oh, yeah.
-And so you return.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.534
What did it feel like
to go back

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:40.767
and you go, "Oh, yeah, I lived
a lot of time in this place"?

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:43.400
-We were -- We were good
when it was time to go.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.534
No, it was really
a beautiful experience

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:48.467
because, you know,
that's a tradition.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.734
You do your official portraits.

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:54.634
The next president is supposed
to invite you back to hang them.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.167
We were never invited back.

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:59.501
So these pictures had been done
for a long, long time.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:02.834
But it's also a chance
for the staff

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:05.501
to come back and reminisce
and to be together.

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:09.133
It's a -- It's a ritual.
So it was good to see everybody.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.834
It was good to see
all of the staff.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:13.534
I mean, as quiet as it's kept,

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.701
my girls lived
in the White House

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.968
longer they lived any house.
-Yeah.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:19.434
-So that's where they grew up.

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:23.501
So to go back and to see all
the staff that are still there,

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:26.033
to see all the people
that they grew up with,

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:27.334
it was really --

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:28.968
Well, the girls weren't there
at the time,

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:31.267
but it was good for
Barack and I to see everyone.

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:33.033
-Do you ever have dreams
that you still live there?

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:36.367
-Oh! No. Oh, I'm sorry.

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:38.534
I didn't mean to say that
like that.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:42.000
It's like -- No, no, I don't --
I don't have dreams.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.667
-You don't ever go like,
"Oh, yeah, I'll go down

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:48.467
the steps here and do that."
-No. No. Funny story.

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:50.901
At Biden's inauguration,

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:53.701
all the formers gathered,

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:56.000
and they were doing
a public service announcement.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.734
And then we had to leave.

00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:01.200
And this is the first time
Barack attended --

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.234
I think he was there
when somebody else's

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.567
presidential motorcade was out.

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:07.701
So he walks out,
and usually the first car up

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:09.200
is the President, right?

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.367
And he goes walking to the first
car, and his security is like,

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:17.300
"Sir, um, that's not --
that's not your car."

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.701
-Oops.
-He's like, "Oh."

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:21.067
He's like, "Okay.
Well, where do I go?"

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:23.601
So we had to pass
the presidential motorcade,

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:28.200
then the VP, and then we went
way back, and then it was ours.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.801
Because you go
in descending order.

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:32.434
-You're like,
"But I was just..."

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.634
-But the thing was,
we were so glad

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:38.801
to get in that back motorcade
and to go home...

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:40.501
-Yeah.
-...to our house.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:41.868
-To your actual house.

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:44.033
-You know, that's
the progress of democracy.

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:46.167
You do your time,
you pass it on,

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:49.000
you let the next president lead.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:53.000
And so it was --
it's kind of a relief.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.267
-In this book,

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:57.767
there's so many great stories
about your life,

00:02:57.767 --> 00:03:00.567
but there's also tips
on how to deal with

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:03.167
what we're dealing with,
with everything,

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:06.434
with what we all --
isolation with COVID.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:09.634
And just everything is kind of
touched in this book.

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:13.033
And one thing I loved
is "the power of small."

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:16.434
-Yeah, yeah, that's one of
the early chapters because --

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:20.567
I wrote this chapter
particularly for young people

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.834
who are feeling so anxious
about the state of the world.

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.434
I mean, no wonder.

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:28.133
Climate change,
riots on Capitol Hill,

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.167
gun violence, on and on.

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:33.701
And these young kids,
young kids as young as 15,

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:36.133
are trying to figure out
how to solve these problems,

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:37.801
and they're getting all twisted

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.601
because they don't yet
have the power

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:43.033
because they're trying to
bite off too much, too soon.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.400
And so "the power of small"
is to focus

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.634
on what you can
uniquely control.

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.467
And for a kid in high school,

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:52.200
it's graduating
from high school.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.400
You know, get your education
because you can't do that --

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.567
You can't end violence
in your neighborhood

00:03:57.567 --> 00:04:00.601
unless you focus
on what's at hand.

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:03.000
So starting small,
even for us as adults,

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.300
is about focus
on your own knitting

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.167
because there's power in that.

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:09.734
You know, if each of us
just raise the children

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.334
we bring into the world --

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:14.267
you know, if we did nothing else
but do that --

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:17.601
oh, just imagine
where we would be as a nation,

00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:20.434
as a human race,
if we just took care of that,

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:22.701
if we showed them
the love and the focus

00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:24.901
and if we put our time
and energy into that

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:27.767
instead of trying to solve
all the big problems.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.701
So change happens
in small bites.

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:31.167
It's not just the big stuff.

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:32.567
-Yeah, because it starts small,

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:34.267
then it goes to a family,
then it goes to a community.

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:37.300
And it was great.
There's also a chapter

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.667
dedicated to
"when they go low, we go high."

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:44.300
-Well, people
still keep asking me,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.501
"You still mean that?"
-Yeah.

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:50.801
But that was --
that was an epic line.

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:54.968
That was just --
It stuck in everyone's head.

00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:58.100
Did you realize how powerful
that would be years after?

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:02.067
-No, no. I didn't know
I'd be known for that line.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:04.167
But I'm proud of that.

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:07.467
People ask me,
do I still -- do I ever go low?

00:05:07.467 --> 00:05:10.167
And, yeah, I go low.

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:11.701
-You do.
-I go low a lot of times.

00:05:11.701 --> 00:05:14.667
But I think for people
who have a platform,

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:17.801
who are being looked up to,

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:20.501
we have a responsibility
to stay high

00:05:20.501 --> 00:05:23.000
because kids are watching us.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.601
If you need to go low,
go low at home.

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:28.033
Do it with your kitchen table,
with your spouse.

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:32.701
But we set the example,
because leaders set the tone.

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:37.234
And we felt what it felt like
to be led with low,

00:05:37.234 --> 00:05:39.334
and it didn't feel great.

00:05:39.334 --> 00:05:42.534
That's why it's important.
It's a practice. It's a habit.

00:05:42.534 --> 00:05:45.000
It's something we show
the next generation,

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.434
that we don't --
That doesn't mean we settle.

00:05:47.434 --> 00:05:49.167
That doesn't mean
we're complacent.

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:51.200
It means we think
before we speak,

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.934
because words matter,
and I still believe that.

00:05:53.934 --> 00:05:56.934
And I try the best that I can
when I'm in the public eye,

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:59.133
when I know that kids
are watching,

00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:01.934
to stay high
because high begets high.

00:06:01.934 --> 00:06:03.400
-That's right.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:10.334
Now, uh...

00:06:10.334 --> 00:06:12.400
you went on a book tour
around the country,

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.200
and you had
amazing conversations

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.334
with amazing people.

00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:19.133
Our pal Gayle King, who we love.
Tyler Perry.

00:06:19.133 --> 00:06:20.601
-Lots of great people.
-Hoda Kotb.

00:06:20.601 --> 00:06:22.634
-David Letterman.
-David Letterman.

00:06:22.634 --> 00:06:26.000
-Oh, so many.
Sure. Conan O'Brien. Sure.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.734
-Alright. Alright.
You were busy.

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:30.400
-Yeah, yeah. It's interesting.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.033
But, you know,
there's always time

00:06:32.033 --> 00:06:35.167
for another book, you know?
Um...

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:36.968
But the list is --
Amazing people.

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:38.767
And you turned it
into a podcast.

00:06:38.767 --> 00:06:40.000
-Yeah.
-And this is great.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.901
It's a great thing.
You have to listen to it.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:44.100
It's such great conversation.
-"The Light Podcast."

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.868
So, for those
who missed the book tour,

00:06:45.868 --> 00:06:47.667
we've recorded
every conversation,

00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:49.567
edited down
to the best of the best.

00:06:49.567 --> 00:06:51.267
And, you know,
it touches on the book,

00:06:51.267 --> 00:06:54.667
but we also each share
our own stories of finding light

00:06:54.667 --> 00:06:56.901
and developing friendships
and relationships.

00:06:56.901 --> 00:06:59.300
It's really a fun
set of conversations

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.234
that are now on Audible.

00:07:01.234 --> 00:07:04.234
-And then you have --
One of the interviews

00:07:04.234 --> 00:07:06.934
or the conversations
are with Oprah Winfrey.

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:09.701
-The one and only.
-Yeah. Oprah Winfrey.

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:11.300
And it airs --
-That Oprah.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.067
-That Oprah.

00:07:13.067 --> 00:07:15.734
And it's airing on April 25th
on Netflix as a special.

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:19.000
-Yeah, that will be televised
because when you're with Oprah,

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.801
you just televise it.

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:22.501
-I just feel like, yeah,
you have to televise it.

00:07:22.501 --> 00:07:24.334
Yeah, but you have
actually become friends

00:07:24.334 --> 00:07:26.634
with Oprah Winfrey.
You guys are really --

00:07:26.634 --> 00:07:29.734
-I mean, Oprah was one of
the very early supporters

00:07:29.734 --> 00:07:32.267
before Barack
was even thinking about running.

00:07:32.267 --> 00:07:35.067
I mean, she spotted him
when he was a U.S. senator.

00:07:35.067 --> 00:07:37.534
And she has sort of been --

00:07:37.534 --> 00:07:41.033
Oprah is that person
who never asks for anything

00:07:41.033 --> 00:07:45.267
but is always there with her
generosity and love and support.

00:07:45.267 --> 00:07:48.267
There isn't anything
you can't ask her to do

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:51.400
if you're a friend
that she won't try to do.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.501
She is who she appears to be.
-Yeah.

00:07:54.501 --> 00:07:56.467
-And I am lucky
to call her a friend.

00:07:56.467 --> 00:07:58.634
-I want to show a clip
from your special.

00:07:58.634 --> 00:08:00.501
Here's a look
at "The Light We Carry:

00:08:00.501 --> 00:08:03.033
Michelle Obama
and Oprah Winfrey."

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:04.901
-When you first arrived
in Hawaii,

00:08:04.901 --> 00:08:07.167
you were looking for --
and I understand why --

00:08:07.167 --> 00:08:09.000
You were a working woman
and had never been to Hawaii.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.734
So you're looking for the Hawaii
in "Hawaii Five-0."

00:08:11.734 --> 00:08:13.501
Those of you who remember
that show.

00:08:13.501 --> 00:08:16.434
-Mai Tais
and sunsets on the beach.

00:08:16.434 --> 00:08:19.334
-And honeymoon suites.
-Instead...

00:08:19.334 --> 00:08:22.467
-Yeah, instead, it was a trip
home to visit his family.

00:08:22.467 --> 00:08:24.033
That's where he was from.

00:08:24.033 --> 00:08:26.534
He wasn't going back
to some island vacation.

00:08:26.534 --> 00:08:29.100
He was going back
to be with his people.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:32.834
But I was young and I was --
It was cold in Chicago,

00:08:32.834 --> 00:08:34.901
and I thought, "I'm going
to Hawaii with my man.

00:08:34.901 --> 00:08:36.434
It's going to be so romantic."

00:08:36.434 --> 00:08:38.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.934 --> 00:08:41.067
And then we landed,
and we went straight

00:08:41.067 --> 00:08:43.801
to Toot and Gramps' apartment.
No ocean.

00:08:43.801 --> 00:08:45.901
It was a high-rise building.

00:08:45.901 --> 00:08:48.267
Go up to the 10th floor.
You know, walk in.

00:08:48.267 --> 00:08:50.701
Looks like
my grandparents' house.

00:08:50.701 --> 00:08:53.133
Might as well be on
the South Side of Chicago.

00:08:53.133 --> 00:08:56.834
-[ Laughs ]
It's not reality. I love it.

00:08:56.834 --> 00:08:58.901
Michelle Obama, everybody.

00:08:58.901 --> 00:09:00.267
"The Light We Carry:

00:09:00.267 --> 00:09:02.100
Michelle Obama
and Oprah Winfrey"

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.400
premieres April 25th on Netflix.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:06.434
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:09:06.434 --> 00:09:08.467
Stick around.
Thank you, as always.

